codegraph standalone distributions include Node.js and production npm dependencies.

Node.js is distributed under the MIT license and includes third-party software under the terms recorded in licenses/node/LICENSE inside each standalone archive.

Production npm package license files and package metadata remain in node_modules inside each standalone archive. codegraph itself is licensed under the repository LICENSE file.


Bundled graph viewer libraries

The packaged graph viewer vendors browser builds of graphology, graphology-layout-forceatlas2, and sigma under docs/graph-visualization/vendor/. Full MIT license texts for those bundles are also shipped alongside the assets:

- docs/graph-visualization/vendor/LICENSE.graphology.txt
- docs/graph-visualization/vendor/LICENSE.graphology-layout-forceatlas2.txt
- docs/graph-visualization/vendor/LICENSE.sigma.txt

